During the experiment, we find that the kinds of metal chlorides plays an important role during thermal exfoliation. As we discussed above, the metal ions $\mathrm{\DeltaLi^{+}}$ and $\mathbf{K}^{+}$ ) from molten metal chlorides probably inserted into the crystal layers of 2D ZnZIF-L and unraveled the compact carbon layers during the thermal treatment. To gain deeper insight into the role of the exfoliators of KCl and LiCl, we tried to use individual KCl or LiCl as the exfoliator, and the corresponding products obtained via thermal exfoliation at $800^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ was assigned as NGM-K and NGM-Li, respectively. We figure out that the $\mathrm{K^{+}}$ and $\mathrm{Li^{+}}$ ions play different roles during the thermal treatment. The mixed exfoliator consists of both KCl and LiCl is the key factor to produce NGM-800 (a labelled as NGM-mix in this section). As shown in Figure 3a,b, NGM-K is much thinner and smoother than NGMLi. The NGM-Li nanosheets are thicker than NGM-K nanosheets, as roughly observed by SEM in Figure S11a,c, and there are richer pores on the surface of NGM-Li nanosheet (Figure S11b,d).
The different roughness are expected to bring a d porosity in NGM-Li and NGM-K. According to adsorption-desorption isotherms (Figure 3c) and pore size distributions (Figure 3d), NGM-Li have a higher proportion of mesopores than NGM-K, which is in accordance with the rough and porous surface as observed by SEM images (Figure 3 b). We suppose that although either $\mathrm{K^{+}}$ or $\mathrm{Li^{+}}$ is able to unravel the carbon layers, the $\mathrm{K^{+}}$ ions are likely more effective in intercalation and exfoliation through intercalation-expansion-microexplosion in $Z\mathrm{n}$ -ZIF-L derived carbon. Thus, we guess that $\mathrm{Li^{+}}$ ions might contribute more to etching the carbons to create larger mesopores (ca. $4.0\mathrm{nm}\mathrm{,}$ ). Therefore, after integrating the functionalities of KCl and LiCl, the mixed exfoliator produces the extraordinary NGM-mix (i.e. NGM-800) that consists of ultrathin nanosheets with a plenty of pores on the surface. The atomic scale defectives in NGM-mix will contribute to the formation of abundant active sites.
